NUC
sym_intern_prehashed now properly truncates to name length before hashing
 q)string `$"abc\000def"   / was "abc\000def", now "abc"

FIX
the compiler-warning sweep: size bounds for -Walloc-size-larger-than, -Wformat-truncation (q_kapi.c, q_handles.c, q_kafka.c) and explicit inits for -Wmaybe-uninitialized (q_adverb.c, q_duckdb.c)

improved `date$ on a timestamp vector: the vectorized numeric-cast worker was a per-element boxed cast (collection_elem + dispatch + an atom per cell)
 q)\t `date$12000000?.z.p    / was 1260, now 135

improved `d[ks]` on tuple-keyed dictionaries, and `x?y` on a general-list x: the domain's keys are hashed once and each probe is O(1), was a linear atom_eq scan per probe, ~100x slower than kdb
